    <!-- Unit Overview -->
    <section class="welcome-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-compass section-icon"></i> Unit Overview</h2>
        <p>This unit moves from data storage to the mechanics of logic. It explores how programs make decisions (Selection), repeat tasks (Iteration), and organise logic into Modules. It also introduces the formal analysis of efficiency through Big O Notation and the necessity of Persistent Storage via File I/O.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Syllabus Links -->
    <section class="content-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-bookmark section-icon"></i> What You'll Learn</h2>
        <div class="learning-points">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    B2.3: Sequencing, Selection (If/Elif/Else), and Looping (Count-controlled vs Conditional).
                </li>
                <li>
                    B2.4: Algorithmic efficiency (Big O), Search algorithms (Linear, Binary), and Sort algorithms (Bubble, Selection).
                </li>
                <li>
                    B2.5: File processing (Read, Write, Append) using Python’s native functions.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

